## Overview

The "owner identity" system lives almost entirely in `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/`, with the response projection in the MapStruct `OwnerMapper`, the wire contract in `openapi.yml`, and tests under `src/test/.../acceptance/`.

Important high-level finding: the current implementation is a **V1 (flat) shape** — `memberId`, `householdId`, `identityKey` are top-level fields, there is **no `apiVersion` field, no nested `identity` object, and no `schemaVersion` on the audit event**. The one acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.java`) asserts a **V2 target contract** (`apiVersion == 2`, identity fields nested under `$.identity`, and removed from top level) that the production code does **not** yet satisfy.

---

## 1. Region code derivation (e.g. 'NSW')

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/OwnerMemberId.java` — the `region(postcode, city)` method is the authoritative deriver. It looks up the postcode against inclusive ranges (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099); if absent/out-of-range it falls back to the city table (Sydney→NSW, Melbourne→VIC, Brisbane→QLD), else `UNKNOWN`. It also holds `regionForCity`, `postcodeRange`, and `regionOf(id)` (reads the leading letters back out of a member id).

```java
public static String region(String postcode, String city) {
    if (postcode != null) {
        try {
            int value = Integer.parseInt(postcode.trim());
            for (Map.Entry<String, int[]> entry : REGION_POSTCODES.entrySet()) {
                int[] range = entry.getValue();
                if (value >= range[0] && value <= range[1]) {
                    return entry.getKey();
                }
            }
        } catch (NumberFormatException ex) { /* fall back to city table */ }
    }
    return CITY_REGION.getOrDefault(city, "UNKNOWN");
}
```
(Full contents of this file pasted in section 2 below since it is the memberId file.)

---

## 2. householdId, identityKey, memberId derivation

Three dedicated utility classes, each keeping its format in one place:

**`householdId`** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerHouseholdId.java`: first 12 hex chars of `SHA-256(normalizedLastName + '|' + postcode)`; last name trimmed, internal whitespace collapsed, lower-cased; postcode trimmed. Assigned by `AssignHousehold.java` (`owner.setHouseholdId(OwnerHouseholdId.of(owner))`).

**`identityKey`** — `/home/daniel/sandbox/.../owner/OwnerIdentity.java`: `SHA-256` hex of `normalizedE164Telephone + '|' + (email lower-cased or empty) + '|' + soundex(lastName)`. Whole-key equality defines a hard duplicate.

